[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040271544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5040271544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5040271544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLGxwuA","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T23:55:57Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T19:54:49Z","body":"I like the feature – cleans up a lot of noise! \r\n\r\nI am on the fence with propagate… I wonder if `ERR_RETURN` is a little neater, since it uses the same terminology as the language keyword \"return\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040271544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5043645380","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5043645380","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5043645380,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLJ_rxA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T08:31:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T11:54:15Z","body":"The main reason I didn't go with `ERR_RETURN` is that it might seem like it _always_ returns. \r\nThat being said, I agree with the reasons against `ERR_PROPAGATE` too and I'd be totally OK with `ERR_RETURN`!\r\n\r\nEdit: Another option would be `GUARD_OK`, in reference to swift-like guards. Would probably also be easy to understand.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5043645380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5050848776","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5050848776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5050848776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLQ3WCA","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T19:59:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T20:00:23Z","body":"> Edit: Another option would be `GUARD_OK`, in reference to swift-like guards. Would probably also be easy to understand.\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce `GUARD_OK` is nice too – it was also instantly familiar to me, having written a lot of Swift.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5050848776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5057210198","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5057210198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5057210198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLW7nVg","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T10:12:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T10:12:28Z","body":"+1 to naming it GUARD_OK. ERR_RETURN indeed sounds like it always return and ERR_PROPAGATE has me (non-native English) go... \"what does it propagate and where to?\"","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5057210198/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5057248180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5057248180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5057248180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLW97tA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T10:16:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T10:16:07Z","body":"Sounds good to me! I also prefer `GUARD_OK` over the other options, so that's a 3-0-0. So I've switched the PR to that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5057248180/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060108314","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5060108314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5060108314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLZsgGg","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T15:13:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T15:15:15Z","body":"My 2c on `GUARD_OK` bikeshedding :grimacing:\r\nThis is a common idiom; we shouldn't reinvent the ~wheel~ name.\r\n\r\nI did a bit of research on how C++ libraries name it:\r\n\r\n- Google/Android: [`RETURN_IF_ERROR`](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/native/%2B/d4fd864960/libs/ui/include_private/ui/FlattenableHelpers.h#26) \r\n- Google/Chromium: [`RETURN_IF_ERROR`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/%2B/refs/tags/129.0.6646.0/base/types/expected_macros.h#94)\r\n- LLVM: [`RETURN_IF_ERROR` + `UNWRAP_OR_RETURN`](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/llvm/lib/Object/WindowsResource.cpp#L28-L42), and [related proposal](https://lists.llvm.org/pipermail/llvm-commits/Week-of-Mon-20240520/1365129.html)\r\n- Abseil: [`ABSL_RETURN_IF_ERROR`](https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/blob/master/absl/status/status_macros.h#L89-L90)\r\n- Mozilla/Firefox: [`MOZ_TRY`](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/source/mfbt/Try.h#27-34)\r\n- Boost: [`BOOST_OUTCOME_TRY`](https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/latest/libs/outcome/doc/html/reference/macros/tryv.html)\r\n\r\nFurthermore, this idiom has been implemented or proposed in several languages:\r\n- C++ proposal: [`operator try()`](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2017/p0779r0.pdf)\r\n- C++ proposal: [`e.try?`](https://www9.open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2023/p2561r2.html)\r\n- Go proposal: [`try(...)`](https://www.github.com/golang/go/issues/32437)\r\n- Rust implemented: [`try!(...)`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.try.html) -- now replaced with `?` operator \r\n- Swift implemented: [`try ...`](https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/documentation/the-swift-programming-language/errorhandling#Handling-Errors)\r\n- Zig implemented: [`try ...`](https://ziglang.org/documentation/master/#try) \r\n\r\nThere is **overwhelming prior art for \"try\"** (and to a lesser degree \"return if error\"). Furthermore, \"guard\" is often used in RAII contexts such as \"scope guard\" or \"lock guard\". Godot itself already has many uses of \"guard\" with subtly different semantics: \r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/30a0296cc25d7d62fd16e6f9ed5977c6c0ec0e3c/scene/main/node.h#L935-L947\r\n\r\nSo I'd vote to reconsider `GUARD_OK` as a greenfield name.\r\nSince most error-handling macros begin with `ERR_`, maybe simply something like `ERR_TRY`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060108314/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060134462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5060134462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5060134462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLZuGPg","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T15:16:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T15:16:20Z","body":"Good point. ERR_TRY is even better in light of the overwhelming amount of languages using some sort of try","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060134462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060270707","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5060270707","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5060270707,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLZ2acw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T15:29:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T15:45:02Z","body":"That's a good basis for a decision. \r\n\r\n`RETURN_IF_ERR` is unmistakeable if a bit clunky.\r\n`TRY` evokes error handling in a way most languages do. Arguably it could be mistaken with exceptions, but anyone working with Godot knows we don't use those.\r\nHowever `ERR_TRY` evokes a loud failure for me. I think that would be a solid contender for a function that loudly fails on error and returns, but I'd avoid it for the silent one introduced here. (edit: or maybe `TRY_FAIL`? 😅)\r\n\r\n(Personally still prefer `GUARD_OK` by sound but I think being recognisable and unambiguous is the most important thing)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060270707/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060735005","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5060735005","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5060735005,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLaSwHQ","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T16:15:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T16:15:06Z","body":"My two cents here is that you should avoid the `ERR` abbreviation outright in the name. It implies that the macro checks for a **boolean** value_, fails \"loudly\", and returns, because that's what the other macros prefixed with `ERR_` do. The macro added in this PR does not check for a boolean, and does not fail loudly, so it should not be clumped up among these.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5060735005/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5062914423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5062914423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5062914423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLcXxdw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T20:12:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T20:18:55Z","body":"Ok here's a more comprehensive idea for \"the rest\" (though i'm not sure I actually want all those; see below):\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nError some_func() { return ERR_FAILED; }\r\n\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); if (err) { return err; }\r\nTRY(some_func())  // Silently return\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); if (err) { return value; }\r\nTRY_V(some_func(), value)  // Returns value\r\n\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); ERR_FAIL_COND_V(err, err);\r\nTRY_FAIL(some_func())  // Prints: \"ERR_FAILED: some_func()\"\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(err, err, \"The call failed\");\r\nTRY_FAIL_MSG(some_func(), \"The call failed\")  // Prints: \"ERR_FAILED: The call failed\"\r\n\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); ERR_FAIL_COND_V(err, value);\r\nTRY_FAIL_V(some_func(), value)  // Returns value, prints: \"ERR_FAILED: some_func()\"\r\n// Current: Error err = some_func(); ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(err, value, \"The call failed\");\r\nTRY_FAIL_V_MSG(some_func(), value, \"The call failed\")  // Returns value, prints: \"ERR_FAILED: The call failed\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe fundamental difference is: The regular `ERR_` macros booleanize to `true` and ignore the value of the `Error`, while the `TRY` ones default to returning the error, and printing the exact error enum value too, adding free context.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if I'd actually add all of these - god knows we have enough `ERR_` macros already. But I think it's interesting to think about how the naming scheme connects to the macros we already have.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5062914423/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194317304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5194317304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5194317304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNZr9-A","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T16:14:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T16:14:26Z","body":"We discussed this in the core meeting.\r\n\r\nThere is some consensus that we should add this to standardize error handling, and encourage silent error returns (the default `Error` returning form).\r\n\r\nThe naming bikeshed was difficult to paint; for now I consider `RETURN_IF_ERROR` to be the stronger consensus. The main reasons are that it's less of a gotcha than `TRY`, and doesn't introduce any new \"keywords\" to our codebase. `RETURN_IF_ERROR` is very unambiguous to what it does.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194317304/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194754075","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#issuecomment-5194754075","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121617","id":5194754075,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNaGoGw","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T16:56:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T16:56:26Z","body":"In spite of any chosen final name, @lawnjelly 's `THROW_UP` will forever live in my head rent-free.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194754075/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":8,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https: